<h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Try the AI Contact Centre (Council Reception)</h1>

<div class="govuk-panel govuk-panel--confirmation ndx-walkthrough-value-prop">
  <h2 class="govuk-panel__title">
    30 minutes to dial a real council and watch one case capture both your call and your photo
  </h2>
  <div class="govuk-panel__body">
    Dial the +44 800 number provisioned in your sandbox, watch a multi-intent triage cap at four issues, send a photo on the WhatsApp simulator, then dial back and hear: "I've reviewed your photo; environmental health will visit Wednesday, ref ABC123."
  </div>
</div>

<div class="govuk-inset-text ndx-walkthrough-reassurance">
  <strong class="govuk-!-font-size-24">This demo is in English.</strong>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    We explore the Welsh-language gaps and what AWS would need to build for Welsh-speaking residents in <a href="/walkthroughs/ai-contact-centre/step-7/" class="govuk-link">Step 7</a>. The procurement-leverage page is the keepsake.
  </p>
</div>

<p class="govuk-body">
  This scenario provisions a full Amazon Connect contact centre with a real UK +44 800 toll-free number, an en_GB Lex bot, Bedrock Knowledge Base + Guardrails, multimodal photo describe, Connect Cases, Customer Profiles, Contact Lens with PII redaction, a Kinesis stream of redacted segments, a CloudFront-fronted three-pane companion SPA, and AWS WAF. Two demonstrable journeys: distress + multi-intent triage on a real PSTN call, and cross-channel single-case unification when the resident later sends a photo on WhatsApp.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">What you'll do</h2>

<p class="govuk-body-l">In this 30-minute walkthrough, you'll:</p>

<ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number govuk-list--spaced">
  <li><strong>Dial in</strong>, call the +44 800 number from your phone, walk a happy-path bin script, hear Polly read back a reference (5 minutes)</li>
  <li><strong>Distress + multi-intent</strong>, play a layered distressing script and watch the bot cap at 4 intents (5 minutes)</li>
  <li><strong>WhatsApp simulator</strong>, attach a photo, watch Bedrock describe it (4 minutes)</li>
  <li><strong>One case, two channels (the climax)</strong>, dial back and hear "I've reviewed your photo; environmental health will visit Wednesday, ref ABC123." (5 minutes)</li>
  <li><strong>Sentiment + safeguarding</strong>, inspect the redacted transcript pane (4 minutes)</li>
  <li><strong>BYO WhatsApp + cleanup</strong>, read the BYO-WABA path, tear down with isb close-account (4 minutes)</li>
  <li><strong>What we'd need from AWS to make this Welsh-ready</strong>, the keepsake (3 minutes)</li>
</ol>

